{
  "_note": [
    "Indicator terms grouped by language. Every list is checked against every prompt no",
    "matter what LANG says: people swear in their first language with their locale set to",
    "en_US. This is data, not a locale file - UI strings live in locales/*.json.",
    "",
    "What's in: real profanity, and vulgar insults used as profanity.",
    "What's out, on purpose:",
    "  - Minced oaths and mild interjections. OMG, darn, heck, gosh, jeez, shoot, crikey,",
    "    天啊, あら, 어머 are not swearing. Nor are sv jäklar, tl putragis, uk бляха-муха,",
    "    id kampret, es gilipuertas, it mannaggia - each is the softened form of a real",
    "    swear that is already listed.",
    "  - Insults that are merely rude: idiot, stupid, ja てめえ, ko 닥쳐, zh 廢話.",
    "  - Racial and ethnic slurs. Targeted hate speech, not frustration at a build.",
    "  - Anything that appears inside an innocent word. Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Thai",
    "    and Bopomofo have no spaces, so those terms are matched as substrings and a",
    "    collision is permanent. Excluded for that reason: 幹 (幹嘛/骨幹/樹幹), 操 (操作),",
    "    我靠 (我靠近), 三小 (三小時), 媽的 (我媽的電話), ばか (ばかり), カス (カスタム),",
    "    ボケ (写真がボケる), しね (動作しねぇ), 시발 (시발점), 씹 (씹다), 졸라 (졸라대다),",
    "    새끼 (강아지 새끼), หี (หีบ), แม่ง (แม่งาน), 柒 (柒佰元), 鳩 (斑鳩), 屁 (屁股),",
    "    撚 (撚手小菜 - the compounds 好撚/唔撚/撚樣 are listed instead).",
    "  - Anything that is an ordinary word in another language, because all lists match at",
    "    once: en git/hoe/fag/sod, fr con/bite/cul, de Mist, sv fan/skit, es coger/concha,",
    "    tr mal, nl kanker/tering/eikel/doos/naai, hi साला, bg кур, ro morții.",
    "  - Two-letter ASCII abbreviations that collide with real acronyms: bc, mc, sb, tmd,",
    "    vl, aq. e04, on9, nmsl, vcl, amk, bkl and fdp are unambiguous and stay.",
    "",
    "test-indicators.py enforces all of the above. Run it after editing."
  ],
  "_english_homographs": {
    "_why": [
      "test-indicators.py fails any non-English term that is also in /usr/share/dict/words,",
      "because every list runs against every prompt and a Swedish term that is an English",
      "word turns every English prompt into a false positive. These nine are the accepted",
      "exceptions: each is archaic, taxonomic or a loanword nobody types in English, while",
      "the swear itself is common in its own language. A NEW collision still fails."
    ],
    "bordel": "fr - English 'bordel' is an archaic spelling of bordello",
    "cony": "ca - English 'cony' is an archaic word for rabbit",
    "foder": "pt - English 'foder' is an obsolete dialect form",
    "hoer": "nl - English 'hoer' is an obsolete spelling",
    "hure": "de - English 'hure' is an obsolete spelling",
    "perse": "et - English 'perse' is an archaic name for a dark blue cloth",
    "pinche": "es - English 'pinche' is the Spanish loanword for a kitchen hand",
    "sial": "ms - English 'sial' is the geological silica-aluminium layer",
    "sitta": "et - English 'Sitta' is the nuthatch genus"
  },
